Open Vanilla 0031: Hero IDs, the public half of a Hero Key, and signing in without sending the key.

A Hero Key's secret (ovk1.<id>.<32 bytes>) now also makes an Ed25519 key pair, the same way
everywhere (the Legend standard): seed = HKDF-SHA256(the secret's 32 bytes, salt
"openvanilla-hero-v1", info "ed25519-seed", 32 bytes), then RFC 8032 Ed25519 from that seed. The
public key, written "ovh1." + base64url, is the Hero ID. It is safe to show: it proves a Legend is
yours without giving away the key. Test vector (auth::herokey::tests::hero_id_test_vector): secret
bytes 00..1f gives ovh1.GVSN6lA0SzCD8nQfZIyrChuVy5ERLpDJNQT1xssI-Sg, and its signature of
"openvanilla-hero-v1\nchallenge:abc" is
N-HLEYmR5g_4FCo_me8yAcKGnFyzI2zaH9K0paTp1zG4itrnvcjtF9CtCh1do9HWOQXvKT81o2C7K0mE3usdCA.

Stored (migration 0031_hero_id.sql): hero_keys.hero_pub (the 32-byte public key, filled when a key
is made and on the next key sign-in for older keys; the secret is still never stored),
users.hero_public (opt-in, off by default) and hero_challenges (sign-in challenges: 5 minutes, used
once). The key page shows "Your Hero ID" under the key, with Copy, one line on what it is, and
"Show my Hero ID on my Legends" (POST /account/hero/public, form token); a key with no Hero ID yet
says "Sign in with your Hero Key once to see your Hero ID."

Sign-in without the secret: on /key, a browser with WebCrypto Ed25519 makes the Hero ID in the page,
gets GET /api/hero/challenge, signs "openvanilla-hero-v1\nchallenge:<challenge>" and POSTs only
{key_id, hero, challenge, sig} to /auth/hero (same-site only, the same per-network and per-key
counters as /auth/key). The realm finds the working key, checks the Hero ID matches, verifies the
signature, uses up the challenge and signs in exactly as /auth/key does. Without Ed25519, or for a
key with no Hero ID yet, the page sends the key with the old form (which then fills the Hero ID).

For other sites: GET /api/heroes.json lists {account, username, hero} for players who chose to
show their Hero ID and have a working key with one ("account" is the game (realmd) account id of
their game account, null while the game database can't be reached; cached 60 s, open to any site).
POST /api/hero/verify {hero, message, sig} answers {"ok": true|false}: a pure signature check, no
account lookup, limited per network, allowed from any site (no cookies, nothing changes).
New crates: hkdf 0.12 (already in the lock) and ed25519-dalek 2.
